inputs.description:
Use FloatsToBuffer or Ints to buffer to pass additional input params, define in AdditionalCode for example:

cbuffer AdditionalIntParams : register(b2)
{
    int Index;
}
cbuffer AdditionalFloatParams : register(b3)
{
    float4 Color;
}

Use SamplerState node to add custom sampler(s); first sampler input is defined in template as CustomSampler.
samplers coming after that will need to be defined in AdditionalCode, for example:

sampler Sampler2 : register(s2);

inputs.defaultValue:
float4 noise = hash41u(vertexIndex);
float3 pos = v.Position;
float4 f = GetField( float4(pos, 0));
float4 fColor = GetField( float4(pos, 1));

v.Position +=  A * (noise - 0.5) * f.w;

// Attributes: vel, col, pos, idx 

// Very simple examples:
float3 vp = pos - Offset;
float d = length(vp);
float f = smoothstep(A,B+1,d);
vel-= vp/(d+0.0001);

// f - normalized position in buffer
// p - current point defined as SourcePoints[idx]

float t= Biased( frac((f * (B+1) + A)) );
float3 pForward = qRotateVec3(float3(0,0,1), p.Rotation);

p.Position += pForward * (t -0.5);
p.Position.y += sin(t*2*PI);
p.Color = SampleGradient(t);
p.Scale += t;

